--- title The typeset predicates
--- about A typeset names a family of datatypes, and each one has a
--- about question that asks whether a value belongs to it. Rebol's own
--- about library leans on SERIES? in particular: REJOIN branches on it,
--- about and without it that function cannot run at all.

--- id typesets/a-block-is-a-series
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
series? [1]
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-string-is-a-series
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
series? "a"
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-binary-is-a-series
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note All three, which is what the family means and what a native
--- note taking a series has to accept.
--- code
series? #{01}
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-number-is-not-a-series
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
series? 1
--- result
#(false)

--- id typesets/nothing-is-not-a-series
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
series? none
--- result
#(false)

--- id typesets/a-file-counts-as-a-string
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note The family is wider than the datatype: a file, a url, an email
--- note and a tag are all any-string.
--- code
any-string? %a
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-block-is-not-a-string
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
any-string? [1]
--- result
#(false)

--- id typesets/a-paren-counts-as-a-block
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
any-block? first [(1)]
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-set-word-counts-as-a-word
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
any-word? first [a:]
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-string-is-not-a-word
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
any-word? "a"
--- result
#(false)

--- id typesets/a-native-counts-as-a-function
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
any-function? :add
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-number-is-scalar
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
scalar? 1
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-string-is-not-scalar
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
scalar? "a"
--- result
#(false)

--- id typesets/a-path-counts-as-a-path
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
any-path? first ['a/b]
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/a-typeset-built-from-a-block-of-datatypes
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note A typeset need not be one of the named families: code can make
--- note its own out of whichever datatypes it cares about. Rebol's own
--- note base-defs.reb builds one per generated function this way.
--- code
mold to typeset! [integer! string!]
--- result
"make typeset! [integer! string!]"

--- id typesets/asking-whether-a-datatype-is-in-a-built-typeset
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
find to typeset! [integer!] integer!
--- result
#(true)

--- id typesets/what-a-built-typeset-reports-itself-as
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
type? to typeset! [integer!]
--- result
#(typeset!)
